#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1122
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <Poll>poll</Poll> names the <GroupRole>roles</GroupRole> that vote, that see the results and that see the details, and the organizer and those who manage polls always see them. Once a <PollBallot>ballot</PollBallot> is in, what voters saw no longer changes, except the deadline. One account gives one vote, whichever of its profiles it uses, and a profile several accounts share votes on its own. A secret poll keeps no answers on its ballots, only the count of each <PollOption>answer</PollOption> grows, so neither the group's admins nor an app can see who voted for what. No counts show before its end, and a finished one is not opened again. A public poll also takes the votes of signed-in non-members of a public group. Deleting the <Value>value</Value> that carries a poll deletes the poll."
msgstr "<Poll>Glasanje</Poll> navodi <GroupRole>uloge</GroupRole> koje glasaju, koje vide rezultate i koje vide detalje, a organizator i oni koji upravljaju glasanjima ih vide uvek. Kad stigne prvi <PollBallot>listić</PollBallot>, ono što su glasači videli više se ne menja, osim roka. Jedan nalog daje jedan glas, kojim god svojim profilom, a profil koji deli više naloga glasa posebno. Tajno glasanje ne čuva odgovore na listićima, raste samo broj glasova svakog <PollOption>odgovora</PollOption>, pa ni admini grupe ni aplikacija ne vide ko je za šta glasao. Brojevi se ne vide pre kraja, a završeno se ne otvara ponovo. Javno glasanje prima i glasove prijavljenih nečlanova javne grupe. Brisanje <Value>vrednosti</Value> koja nosi glasanje briše i glasanje."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1146
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A new <Group>group</Group> can start from a preset: chat, folder, announcements, feed, polls, form, map or page. A preset sets what any group can have, so all of it can be changed later. The group keeps only the preset's name: its avatar shows that kind while the group still fits it, and the list of sub-groups can be narrowed to one kind. Announcements also get a <GroupManifest>manifest</GroupManifest> of their own, in which `everyone` no longer writes. A feed is two groups, one with the Feed app and one below it with FeedCreator, and each keeps its own copy of its app, so a new version reaches only the feeds made after it. A group for polls, a form and a map keep a copy of their app the same way, and a form gets its two groups for files only once it needs them. The root offers no map, as it has one of its own."
msgstr "Nova <Group>grupa</Group> može da krene od preseta: chat, folder, obaveštenja, feed, glasanja, forma, mapa ili stranica. Preset podešava ono što svaka grupa može da ima, pa se sve može kasnije promeniti. Grupa pamti samo ime preseta: njen avatar pokazuje tu vrstu dok joj grupa još odgovara, a lista podgrupa može da se suzi na jednu vrstu. Obaveštenja dobijaju i sopstveni <GroupManifest>manifest</GroupManifest>, u kom `everyone` više ne piše. Feed su dve grupe, jedna sa aplikacijom Feed i jedna ispod nje sa FeedCreator-om, i svaka čuva svoju kopiju aplikacije, pa nova verzija stiže samo u feed-ove napravljene posle nje. Grupa za glasanja, forma i mapa na isti način čuvaju kopiju svoje aplikacije, a forma svoje dve grupe za fajlove dobija tek kad joj zatrebaju. Koren ne nudi mapu, jer ima svoju."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:934
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A new value reaches right away, with no refresh, everyone who has the app open and may see it."
msgstr "Nova vrednost odmah stiže, bez osvežavanja, svakome ko ima otvorenu aplikaciju i sme da je vidi."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:952
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An app can keep its <Value>values</Value> under rules its editors set: which <GroupRole>roles</GroupRole> write and which read everything, one answer per person, changing one's own answer, a deadline, anonymous answers and, in a public group, answers from signed-in non-members. Potok also scores a quiz by a key only the editors see, counts the answers for a summary, keeps the files sent with them in two sub-groups of the app's group, and sends a push about each new answer to whoever asks for it. That is how a group becomes a form."
msgstr "Aplikacija može da čuva svoje <Value>vrednosti</Value> po pravilima koja postave njeni urednici: koje <GroupRole>uloge</GroupRole> upisuju, a koje čitaju sve, jedan odgovor po osobi, izmena svog odgovora, rok, anonimni odgovori i, u javnoj grupi, odgovori prijavljenih nečlanova. Potok uz to boduje kviz po ključu koji vide samo urednici, broji odgovore za rezime, fajlove poslate uz odgovore čuva u dve podgrupe grupe aplikacije i javlja svaki nov odgovor onome ko to zatraži. Tako grupa postaje forma."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1176
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An app's data carry their own rules"
msgstr "Podaci aplikacije nose svoja pravila"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1178
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An app's settings are one <Value>value</Value> of its own: the app's data, a secret part only its editors read, and the rules of its other collections, which Potok holds to on every call. A rule names the <GroupRole>roles</GroupRole> that write and those that read everything; everyone else reads only what they wrote, and those who may edit the group always read all. A collection without a rule is closed the same way. One answer per person counts one account once, as a poll does. An answer written while its collection was anonymous never shows its author to anyone but the author, though its time shows, and whoever rewrites the app's code could still get around it. Files sent with answers are values with a <ValueAttachment>file</ValueAttachment> in two sub-groups of the app's group: a closed one, whose members alone open them, and one that inherits the members. Whoever sent a file can always open it."
msgstr "Podešavanja aplikacije su jedna njena <Value>vrednost</Value>: podaci aplikacije, tajni deo koji čitaju samo njeni urednici i pravila ostalih njenih kolekcija, kojih se Potok drži pri svakom pozivu. Pravilo imenuje <GroupRole>uloge</GroupRole> koje upisuju i one koje čitaju sve. Svi ostali čitaju samo ono što su sami upisali, a oni koji smeju da uređuju grupu uvek čitaju sve. Kolekcija bez pravila je zatvorena na isti način. Jedan odgovor po osobi broji jedan nalog jednom, kao kod glasanja. Odgovor upisan dok je kolekcija bila anonimna nikome osim autoru ne pokazuje ko ga je napisao, mada se vidi kada je poslat, a ko prepiše kod aplikacije mogao bi to da zaobiđe. Fajlovi poslati uz odgovore su vrednosti sa <ValueAttachment>fajlom</ValueAttachment> u dve podgrupe grupe aplikacije: zatvorenoj, čiji ih članovi jedini otvaraju, i onoj koja nasleđuje članove. Onaj ko je fajl poslao uvek može da ga otvori."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:950
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Collects answers by its own rules"
msgstr "Skuplja odgovore po svojim pravilima"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:925
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Each app has its own <Value>values</Value>, apart from the other apps of the group. It can search them, sort them, count them, add them up and read them page by page, the newest first if it likes."
msgstr "Svaka aplikacija ima svoje <Value>vrednosti</Value>, odvojene od ostalih aplikacija u grupi. Može da ih pretražuje, sortira, broji, sabira i čita po stranicama, ako hoće i od najnovijih."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:943
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "It can also read the values of the group's other apps, except those kept under rules, and it writes only to its own."
msgstr "Može da čita i vrednosti ostalih aplikacija u grupi, osim onih koje se čuvaju po pravilima, a upisuje samo u svoje."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1055
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Members read and save values, and so do signed-in non-members where an app's rules open that to them in a public group. Rules can narrow it further, and the number of saves is limited."
msgstr "Vrednosti čitaju i upisuju članovi, a u javnoj grupi i prijavljeni nečlanovi, kad im to pravila aplikacije otvore. Pravila to mogu i dalje da suze, a broj upisa je ograničen."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:749
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only app data has a collection, named with small letters, digits, - and _."
msgstr "Kolekciju ima samo podatak aplikacije, a ime joj je od malih slova, cifara, - i _."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1059
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Potok checks who answers, when, how many times and how much, not what an answer says."
msgstr "Potok proverava ko odgovara, kada, koliko puta i koliko, a ne šta odgovor kaže."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1170
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The default description and every <GroupAltDescription>alternative description</GroupAltDescription> can be an app. Its data are <Value>values</Value> marked as data, and each of them knows which app it belongs to and which of the app's collections holds it. A composite key holds them in the same group, and deleting an alternative description deletes its data too."
msgstr "Podrazumevani opis i svaki <GroupAltDescription>alternativni opis</GroupAltDescription> mogu da budu aplikacija. Njeni podaci su <Value>vrednosti</Value> označene kao podaci, a svaka zna kojoj aplikaciji pripada i koja je kolekcija aplikacije drži. Složeni ključ ih drži u istoj grupi, a brisanje alternativnog opisa briše i njegove podatke."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:256
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "anonymous when written"
msgstr "anonimno pri upisu"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:255
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "collection of app data"
msgstr "kolekcija podataka aplikacije"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:257
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "revision"
msgstr "revizija"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:258
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "score and grades"
msgstr "bodovi i ocene"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:186
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "ready setup"
msgstr "gotova postavka"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1154
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <Group>group</Group> can have a place: both coordinates or neither, set by whoever may edit it, with a pin picked from a list or the one of its kind, and a picked pin keeps the kind's mark in its corner, as the group's picture does. A map app shows the places of the groups right under its own, each to whoever sees that group. A group added from the map is an ordinary sub-group, made by whoever may make one there. The map's pictures come through Potok, so the map service does not see who is looking. The root has no map app but a map of its own: the places of every group the viewer sees, at any depth, which the server gathers into numbered circles where they stand close, narrowed by the filters of the sub-groups, by the pins the groups show and by when a group appeared or was last written in, at any time until the viewer picks a time frame. A search by a group's name, there and among the sub-groups, takes no notice of diacritics or of a name written in Latin or Cyrillic."
msgstr "<Group>Grupa</Group> može da ima mesto: obe koordinate ili nijednu, koje postavlja onaj ko sme da je uređuje, sa pinom izabranim sa liste ili onim njene vrste, a izabrani pin u uglu zadržava znak vrste, kao i slika grupe. Aplikacija mape prikazuje mesta grupa neposredno ispod svoje, svako onome ko tu grupu vidi. Grupa dodata sa mape je obična podgrupa, koju pravi onaj ko tu sme da napravi podgrupu. Slike mape dolaze preko Potoka, pa servis mapa ne vidi ko gleda. Koren nema aplikaciju mape nego svoju mapu: mesta svih grupa koje gledalac vidi, na bilo kojoj dubini, koja server skuplja u krugove sa brojem gde stoje blizu, sužena filterima podgrupa, pinovima koje grupe pokazuju i vremenom kad je grupa nastala ili kad je u njoj poslednji put pisano, u bilo koje vreme dok gledalac ne izabere period. Pretraga po imenu grupe, tu i među podgrupama, ne mari za kvačice ni za to da li je ime napisano latinicom ili ćirilicom."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1152
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A group can stand on a map"
msgstr "Grupa može da stoji na mapi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:699
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A place on a map has both coordinates, each within its range, or neither."
msgstr "Mesto na mapi ima obe koordinate, svaku u njenom opsegu, ili nijednu."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:979
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "It gets the <Group>groups</Group> right under it that have a place on a map, with the pin each one shows, and whoever may make a sub-group there can add one where they tap. A tap on a pin opens that group's description over the app, where its own app, a form or a poll, works with that group's rights. Among them, groups that cover an area come with their borders and with the areas each place lies in, so the app draws the areas and shows only the groups inside one. That is how a group becomes a map. The root needs no such app: it has a map of its own."
msgstr "Dobija <Group>grupe</Group> neposredno ispod sebe koje imaju mesto na mapi, sa pinom koji svaka pokazuje, a ko tu sme da pravi podgrupe može da doda novu tamo gde dodirne. Dodir na pin otvara opis te grupe preko aplikacije, gde njena aplikacija, forma ili glasanje, radi sa pravima te grupe. Među njima grupe koje pokrivaju područje stižu sa svojim granicama i sa područjima u kojima je svako mesto, pa aplikacija crta područja i pokazuje samo grupe unutar jednog. Tako grupa postaje mapa. Korenu takva aplikacija ne treba: on ima svoju mapu."

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:977
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Shows its groups on a map"
msgstr "Prikazuje svoje grupe na mapi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:187
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "latitude on a map"
msgstr "geografska širina na mapi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:188
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "longitude on a map"
msgstr "geografska dužina na mapi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:189
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "pin on a map"
msgstr "pin na mapi"

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1162
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <Group>group</Group>'s place can be an area instead of a point, as a local community covers its streets: a border drawn on the map or brought from a GeoJSON file, set by whoever may edit the group. The area keeps a pin, which the server puts inside it by itself. An area holds a group when it holds that group's pin, so every place shows the areas around it, smallest first, and an area inside a bigger one lies in it too. Each viewer sees only the areas of the groups they see. On the root's map an area is only the shape of its group: the filters keep it or leave it out like any group, and once it is wide enough it also shows its border, under the pins; a tap on the map lists the areas there, and a filter keeps only the groups inside chosen areas, which stay outlined."
msgstr "Mesto <Group>grupe</Group> može biti područje umesto tačke, kao što mesna zajednica pokriva svoje ulice: granica nacrtana na mapi ili uvezena iz GeoJSON fajla, a zadaje je ko sme da uređuje grupu. Područje zadržava pin, koji server sam stavlja unutar njega. Područje obuhvata grupu kad obuhvata njen pin, pa svako mesto pokazuje područja oko sebe, od najmanjeg, a područje unutar većeg i samo leži u njemu. Svako vidi samo područja grupa koje vidi. Na mapi korena područje je samo oblik svoje grupe: filteri ga zadrže ili izostave kao svaku grupu, a kad je dovoljno široko, pokazuje i svoju granicu, ispod pinova; dodir na mapu nabraja područja na tom mestu, a filter ostavlja samo grupe unutar izabranih područja, koja ostaju uokvirena."

